cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "citecheck: protein-mRNA coupling and artefact diagnostics for CITE-seq data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Elmasnur"
    family-names: "Yılmaz"
    email: "elmasnrylmz@gmail.com"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
keywords:
  - CITE-seq
  - single-cell
  - multimodal
  - quality control
  - post-transcriptional regulation
abstract: >-
  Measures how well each antibody in a CITE-seq experiment is predicted by its
  cognate transcript, and checks the analysis for five artefacts that produce
  confident but false positives: heterogeneous antibody panels, ambient
  contamination, group-size confounding, degenerate p-value distributions and
  saturated bounded values. Ships a 145-entry antibody-to-gene table with
  annotations for documented post-transcriptional mechanisms.
